    "wacc_rationale": "USD flows, USD WACC. Cost of equity 10.0% = 4.2% 10y UST + beta ~1.15 x 5.0% ERP. Pre-tax cost of debt ~5.2% (FY25 interest expense $156M on ~$5.0-5.5B average debt) -> 4.0% after tax at 24%. Market-value weights ~66% equity ($10.5B at the current price) / 34% debt ($5.5B) -> 8.0%. One WACC for all three scenarios: policy, litigation and volume risk are carried in the scenario flows and the 25% bear weight, not in a rate premium.",
    "lease_treatment": "US GAAP operating leases: lease cost (~$102M FY25) already sits inside operating expenses, so EBITDA is post-lease (treatment B equivalent). Operating lease liabilities ($414M at FY25) are EXCLUDED from net debt; total_debt is borrowings incl. finance leases from the balance sheet. lease_cost_pct_path = 0 because the charge is already in the margin.",
    "nci_treatment": "Flows are whole-company (pre-NCI). NCI is small (FY25 NCI share of net income $22.4M, ~1.5% of group NI), so it is deducted once as a stock in the equity bridge: equity NCI $67.8M + redeemable NCI $74.0M at 2026-06-30. No NCI leakage in the flows.",
    "ebitda_definition": "ebitda_margin_path is PRE-SBC EBITDA: XBRL operating income + D&A + SBC. FY25: 1,994.0 + 618.7 + 95.7 = 2,708.4 (15.60% of revenue); H1-26: 15.19%. The CSV EBITDA column (2,612.8) is post-SBC; SBC is then re-charged in the engine via sbc_pct_path, so it is charged once. FY0 tie: EBIT 1,994 - interest 156 + other income ~134 = 1,972 reported pretax; at 24% tax less NCI the modelled NOPAT less after-tax interest ties to $1,511M attributable NI within ~1%.",
    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF component DCF (scenario-weighted), per dcf-methods routing row 'operating company' with the adaptations for leases (US GAAP operating leases inside EBITDA, excluded from net debt) and NCI (bridge deduction). UHS is a US hospital operator (acute care ~63% of revenue, behavioral health ~37%) -- not a bank/REIT/holdco; first valuation, no prior model. FY0 = FY2025 (Dec year-end); anchors refreshed to the Q2-2026 10-Q balance sheet (debt $5,671.9M, cash $138.8M, 2026-06-30). Owner FCF FY25 = reported FCF 849.2 - SBC 95.7 - interest income 0 = $753.6M; interest income not stripped because UHS is net-debt (~2.0x EBITDA). Reported FCF is after ~$156M cash interest; the component build is unlevered (pre-interest) and debt is deducted in the bridge, so interest is charged once. Repurchaser: the flat share count is funded by actual buybacks ($968M FY25, $485M H1-26, ~$978M authorization remaining). FY2026 guidance (Q2 call, 2026-07-28): adjusted EBITDA less NCI $2.61-2.72B (cut ~$50M at midpoint for softer volumes and ~$50M higher PL/GL reserves), capex $0.95-1.10B; base year-1 margin (15.2% pre-SBC) sits at the guidance midpoint. The $535M behavioral-health jury verdict and related litigation are NOT deducted in the bridge (insurance coverage and post-trial reduction unknown from the filings available); they are carried as a bear-case margin and weight risk. Working capital: receivables-heavy, so growth consumes cash (wc_capture -6% of revenue change; FY25 AR rose $318M on $1.54B revenue growth).",
